  "id": "Compound::DB00697 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Tizanidine is implicated in the regulation of Adra2c through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the alpha-adrenergic receptor system. The evidence suggests that Tizanidine binds to Adra2b, which is a subunit of the alpha-adrenergic receptor, and this binding is linked to the participation of Adra2b in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. This activity is ultimately associated with Adra2c, indicating a potential role for Tizanidine in modulating the function of Adra2c. The evidence also highlights that Tizanidine is included in the class of adrenergic alpha2-agonists, which includes Guanabenz, a known inhibitor of Adra2c. This suggests that Tizanidine may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the alpha-adrenergic receptor, potentially influencing Adra2c through receptor activation or modulation. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Tizanidine and Adra2c, emphasizing the role of alpha-adrenergic receptor activity in this relationship.",
